{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1365690-house-rules-for-injuries","id":1365690,"title":"House Rules for Injuries","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-02-06T03:54:17-08:00","id":1365690,"title":"House Rules for Injuries","content":"A set of house rules because the idea of several bruises causing you to get unconscious is not very cinematic as I see.<br /> <b>Unlimited Injury Conditions</b><br /> The same way it works for multiple non lethal conditions and mental stress, Injuries can be unlimited, and their effects can stack and cause the character to be Taken Out.<br /> All damage sources have a Damage Rating (DR), including direct attacks, defined by the attack, as described in the Damage Rating section, bellow.<br /> While indirect damage requires a roll to resist, the fact the character already rolled his defense already represents the act of resisting a direct attack, and so the damage rating of a direct attack can\u2019t be resisted as it happens to a indirect attack.<br /> Once the character receives damage, the damage creates a single injury of a category defined by the DR (the remaining in the case of Indirect Damage), if it\u2019s 1 the injury condition is Bruised, if 2 it\u2019s Injured, if 3 it\u2019s Maimed, 4 or more Taken Out.<br /> It\u2019s possible to have DR 5 or more, meaning that the attack will require more than a simple armor to keep the character in the scene, but yet, there is no further effect except for the ones chosen by the Storyguide.<br /> Characters can use defensive boxes to reduce the impact of some attacks, but it\u2019s a limited resource that not all characters have access. More information on Defensive Boxes section, bellow.<br /> <br /> <b>Damage Rating</b><br /> The damage rating of direct attacks are defined by the stunts the attacker pick, basically Inflict Damage and Critical. Additionally the attacker can take advantage of an existent injury in the target, and make it worse somehow.<br /> <b>Inflict Damage</b> (opponent soft armor): The attack have Damage Rating 1.<br /> <b>Critical </b>(3 successes): Increase the Damage Rating of the attack by 1. This stunt can be added multiple times, stacking the increase in the DR.<br /> <b>Explore Injury</b> (opponent soft armor +1 successes): The attack has Damage Rating equals to the complication of a target\u2019s chosen existent Injury. This stunt don\u2019t creates a new injury, but the existent injury can become worse if the damage rating results a worse injury. If the result is the same category or weaker, there is no change in the injury and no new injury is caused.<br /> <br /> <b>Defensive Boxes</b><br /> While there is no limits to the number of injuries the character can receive, some characters have special resources to reduce the effects of being hit. This resources are special boxes the character have every scene, related to Hard Armor and particularly resistant characters.<br /> Any time the character would receive damage, including indirect damage, it\u2019s possible to reduce the DR by 1 point, doing so marks the box until the end of the scene. If the character have multiple boxes, it\u2019s possible to spend more than one against the same attack. If all the defensive boxes are marked, the character can\u2019t use this option.<br /> There are 5 types of defensive boxes: Cover, Armor, Bruise, Injury and Maim.<br /> Cover and Armor boxes are granted by external sources (or powers) and can reduce the Damage Rating to 0. It can be used only to protect from damage the cover or armor is useful.<br /> Bruise boxes allow the character reduce the DR to a minimum of 1, and can be used against any kind of damage. Any character with Stamina 5 or more gains 1 bruise box.<br /> Injury boxes allow the character reduce the DR to a minimum of 2, and can be used against any kind of damage. Any character with Stamina 3 or more gains 1 injury box.<br /> Maim boxes allow the character reduce the DR to a minimum of 3, and can be used against any kind of damage.<br /> <br /> <b>Armor, Weapon and Indirect Damage Tags</b><br /> A few tags are changed by the changes in the rules.<br /> <b>Armor Tags</b><br /> <b>Hard Armor</b> (1, 3): The working of the tag changes, the user gains one or more armor boxes, same number as the usual rules. More information in Defensive Boxes, above.<br /> <br /> <b>Weapon Tags</b><br /> <b>Brutal</b> (1): The working of the tag is the same, the cost is of the Critical stunt is reduced by 1 (usually to 2).<br /> <b>Non-Lethal</b> (2): The working of the tag is almost same, the Inflict Damage and Critical stunts cause a condition according to the Damage Rating, Stunned with complication 2 if DR 3 or less and Unconscious if at least 4. It\u2019s possible to use Explore Injury only on the Stunned Condition, with initial DR equals to 2. Instead of throwing off the successes, the target throw off the Stunned Condition with a Difficulty 2 Stamina + Resolve roll.<br /> <b>Stun</b> (1): The working of the tag is the same, the Critical and Explore Injury stunts are not available.<br /> <br /> <b>Indirect Damage Tags</b><br /> <b>Continuous</b> (any): Continuous damage will always explore the injuries caused before. When the source will cause damage again, add to the Damage Rating any injury complication caused previously by the same source not recovered yet. For example, the injury caused by the desert heat will get worse for every hour the character don\u2019t resist its effect.<br /> <b>Deadly</b>: Deadly works as usual, but if combined with Continuous, after receiving the first injury, it will get worse every time it causes damage again. For example, first round in the vacuum of space will cause a Bruised condition, second it will become a Injured Condition, third round it will become a Maimed condition and in the forth round the character is taken out. Defensive boxes can be used to reduce Deadly DR to a minimum of 1.<br /> <br /> <b>Edges and Other Powers</b><br /> A few Edges and Gifts are changed by the change in the rules.<br /> <b>Edges</b><br /> <b>Endurance</b>: The working of the Edge changes, the character gains one bruise box. More information in Defensive Boxes, above.<br /> <br /> <b>General Power Effect</b><br /> <b>Additional Bruised Condition Box</b>: The working of the power changes, the character gains 1 bruise box per additional Bruised Condition Box. More information in Defensive Boxes, above.<br /> <b>Additional Injured Condition Box</b>: The working of the power changes, the character gains 1 injury box per additional Injured Condition Box. More information in Defensive Boxes, above.<br /> <b>Additional Maimed Condition Box</b>: The working of the power changes, the character gains 1 maim box per additional Maimed Condition Box. More information in Defensive Boxes, above.<br /> <b>Multiple Injuries with a Single Attack</b>: The additional injuries can be combined, a single injury cause a Bruised Condition, combining 2 cause a Injured, combining 4 a Maimed and combining 6 Taken out. If the power says it marks all the target Condition Boxes, consider the target instead gains a Maimed condition and marks all the armor, bruise, injury and maim boxes.<br /> <br /> <b>Cover</b><br /> The working of cover changes, a cover have a number of cover boxes (same number as the usual rules). More information in Defensive Boxes, above.<br /> <br /> <b>Antagonists</b><br /> Antagonists still don\u2019t receives any Injury condition, instead have a total of defensive boxes equals to the original Health boxes. The number of health boxes marked by an attack is equal to the Damage Rating of the attack, and once all the defensive boxes are marked, any remaining DR takes the antagonist out.<br /> <br /> <b>Recovering and Healing</b><br /> Recovering and healing suffer no changes, except that there is no need to have free lower category boxes to be able to recover a higher category injury.<br /> For example, using First Aid, it\u2019s possible to turn a Maimed Condition into a Injured condition if it was caused that scene, no need to worry about free Injured condition boxes unmarked.<br /> The difficulty to remove the Taken Out condition is defined by the number of other conditions the character have, as described, and so, it may be necessary to recover other injuries before trying to remove the taken out condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 02-16-2020, 06:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T04:24:48-08:00","id":1365694,"title":"","content":"Just a few comments.<br /> <br /> Made a few simulations and the DR to Injury seams nice (and fitting with the indirect damage rules).<br /> <br /> Cover is better now... still not completely happy.<br /> <br /> Antagonists (as you see) still works the same way...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 02-07-2020, 03:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T12:50:01-08:00","id":1366094,"title":"","content":"A few Changes to make it roll better... I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T21:38:23-08:00","id":1366235,"title":"","content":"I see a little Sea seeping into your Trinity....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-08T03:55:40-08:00","id":1366288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Graylion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1365690-house-rules-for-injuries?p=1366235#post1366235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see a little Sea seeping into your Trinity....</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably... I don\u2019t know... so many RPGs are going this way that\u2019s hard to tell... I hope the sea seeping don\u2019t sink the boat when I play...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-08T08:47:26-08:00","id":1366333,"title":"","content":"I will be interested to see how your play goes. I really enjoy storypath and the partial elimination of one-shot kills, I however am less happy with the injury , weapons and armor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-08T17:06:45-08:00","id":1366435,"title":"","content":"As a quick comment<u>,</u> my largest reference for that system is Ars Magica.<br /> <br /> Ars Magica have rules for wounds getting worse over time, as they are in middle age and lack proper medicine. Also the focus of the game is more long term than the scenes we use in Storypath.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T09:43:46-08:00","id":1366579,"title":"","content":"In the end we had no chance to test it this weekend, but we had a quick discussion and some feed back. Also I have a few results from playing around with the rules.<br /> First impression from my friends, it is sounding more complex than the original. But the reason for that is all the things I didn\u2019t change in the game to avoid having to change anything else (naming: hard Armor, Cover and additional injury boxes).<br /> As a general comment we think the part you treat Injuries as regular conditions is good. The fact you don\u2019t need to control the number of injuries and the fact you can use the rules on Scion for \u201cfate damaged\u201d is interesting. The idea of making a condition worse is also interesting, even to be used in other situations.<br /> <br /> Now my simulations.<br /> <br /> As the rules for Antagonists didn\u2019t change, the options for the characters in most scenes didn\u2019t change.<br /> The heroes get a bit though, if the adversary don\u2019t make a first Injured condition (needed to explore Injury properly) soon, the chances are the characters will win the fight with only a bunch of bruises.<br /> Hard Armor have a big impact when dealing with weaklings. If a lucky one get a Injured Condition, reducing it back to bruised makes the characters even more powerful.<br /> The effect of Scale is a big punch. It basically turn any attack into a injured condition and it results in a faster taken out than it would take by the original rules. Armor helps to delay it, but not much.<br /> <br /> Fighting a \u201ccomplete\u201d character (a non-antagonist) have a different feel, it takes longer if no lucky shots. The chance of both sides end up with just a bunch of bruises is huge.<br /> First, you would invest more successes in the critical than you expect, just because you want to reach the next category to explore deeper.<br /> Single shot the target is possible, Absolutely hard, but possible. You need Armor + 6 successes, what is viable, but uncommon.<br /> Hitting hard just to mark an Armor and leaving no injury to explore properly is frustrating, but that\u2019s the feeling Armor should cause anyway.<br /> Staking the complications of multiple injuries when applicable is probably a good option. I tested with unlimited stacking, and it went bad. I think maybe a up to +3 difficulty for only bruised, +4 when there is at least one Injured and +5 when at least one Maimed. I will test later...<br /> <br /> As a final comment, it works fine. It is as hard to explain as the original","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T05:04:20-08:00","id":1368022,"title":"","content":"Updated the text on the original post.<br /> <br /> Also some feedback from a playtest from yesterday.<br /> <br /> Smooth. The players liked the strategic aspect of the Defensive Boxes (a name for unifying the rules), you can chose to let it hit or defend yourself, and can pileup the defense to avoid all damage by the end of the fight.<br /> <br /> Antagonists are resistant, or maybe I pick them too strong, so the small change (3 successes for crit instead of 4, and possibly multiple hits). For weaklings it\u2019s easier, for hard ones it don\u2019t change much, as you don\u2019t get that many extra successes.<br /> <br /> The successes goes to damage more often. But in the end it would go to help others to achieve critics, so basically the same.<br /> <br /> The dice were cruel, I gave a lot of momentum... really...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 02-16-2020, 06:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}